id: ble_unified_framework
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  BLE unified framework updated
label: BLE_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/ble_unified_framework
provides:
- name: ble_unified_framework
source:
- path: src/command_parser.c
- path: src/event_loop.c
- path: src/rsi_common_utils.c
include:
- path: inc
  file_list:
    - path: generic_command_handling.h
    - path: event_loop.h
    - path: rsi_common_utils.h
define:
- name: SLI_SI91X_ENABLE_BLE_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK
requires:
- name: sl_si91x_wireless
- name: ble
template_file:
  - path: templates/ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen.c.jinja
  - path: templates/ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen.h.jinja

template_contribution:
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: ble_unified_framework
      context: |
        ## BLE Unified Framework Component (Si91x Wireless)
        Generic glue layer that powers the BLE Unified architecture. Provides:
        - **Event loop** (`event_loop.c` / `event_loop.h`): a `generic_event_message_t` queue and `generic_task_cb_t` dispatcher (`ble_generic_cb`). Protocol components push events here from their `*_user_event_hdlrs.c` files; the loop drains them on the BLE task.
        - **Generic command handling** (`generic_command_handling.h`): typed command parsing infrastructure used by the autogenerated init/callback wrappers.
        - **Common utilities** (`rsi_common_utils.h`): logging (`LOG_PRINT_D`), connection-id helpers (`rsi_get_ble_conn_id()`, `rsi_add_ble_conn_id()`, `rsi_6byte_dev_address_to_ascii()`), event/queue primitives shared across protocol components.
        - **Autogen** (`ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen.{c,h}.jinja`): SLC consumes `ble_events`, `wrapper_implementations`, `event_mapped_wrapper`, and `ble_unified_init_hooks` template contributions from every selected protocol component to emit `autogen/ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen.c` and `.h`. The result is a single `ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen_init()` call (invoked by `ble_unified`) that registers ALL callbacks for ALL selected components in one place.
        ### When to depend on this component
        Any protocol-extension component (a new GATT profile, custom SMP variant, new advertising mode) MUST `requires: ble_unified_framework` so its `ble_events` and `wrapper_implementations` contributions get picked up by the autogen step.
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Hand-writing `ble_event_hdlr_auto_gen.c` — it is regenerated on every project generation; edits will be lost. Add/modify event mappings via `template_contribution` in your component's `.slcc`.
        - Pushing events to the event loop without first registering an event handler (the `event_id` declared in `ble_events`) — the dispatcher will silently drop the message.
    priority: -5301

